	"General": {
		"Time": "2020-11-12T21:25:11.487Z",
		"Iscps": null,
		"Agency": "CW",
		"Author": "Zulma Cruz-Gomez",
		"Source": "d1d7780d-a31a-4c23-826e-0495a64694bc",
		"Purpose": "74eb3290-7c26-44e2-9232-c4b761bd7cfb",
		"Lastname": "Beran",
		"countyid": "f5214cb2-953e-41a9-a4ad-71341501e2ad",
		"Firstname": "Katie ",
		"Narrative": "<p>Reporter is a CPS worker at Wicomico DSS(443)235-4942</p><p><br></p><p>Reporter: <span style=\"color: black;\">Katie Beran, LMSW</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Child Protective Service</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 153);\">201 Baptist Street</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 153);\">Suite 27</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 51, 153);\">Salisbury, MD 21801</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Casehead:<span style=\"color: black;\"> Ms. Carol Goodnow</span></p><p>7466 East Furnace Branch Road</p><p>Glen Burnie, Maryland 21060</p><p>(410) 599-9105</p><p><br></p><p>Children:<span style=\"color: black;\"> Haylee Farver 5-6-05 and David Goodnow 3-12-12. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Report as follows:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">November 12, 2020</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Anne Arundel County Dept. of Social Services</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">7500 Richie Highway </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Glen Burnie, MD 21061</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">To Whom It May Concern:</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">I am writing this letter as request for services to a family residing in your county. I currently have an open investigation opened with Ms. Jennifer Murray 1-26-77. She is in a relationship with Rodney Farver DOB 12/2/83, who has two children of his own, Haylee Farver 5-6-05 and David Goodnow 3-12-12. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Mr. Farver was arrested on 10/5/20 and remains incarcerated at the Wicomico County Detention Center on charges of assault against Ms. Murray as well as assault on Ms. Murray’s 13 year old daughter. Mr. Farver did not have custody of his two children and had only had them in his care here in Maryland since last year. They were residing with their maternal grandmother, Carol Goodnow 2/19/51, who has legal custody of both children. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">When Ms. Goodnow found out that Mr. Farver was arrested she came and got both children from Ms. Murray. Ms. Goodnow does not plan on returning the children to Wicomico County. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">However, our agency is aware that the children were removed from Ms. Goodnow’s care last year due to the living conditions of her home. She was said to be living in a trailer that was unsafe for the children. I am aware that Ms. Goodnow has relocated but is now living in an assisted living home where she is not able to keep these children long term. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Ms. Goodnow has informed me that she has intentions on keeping these children with her and is hoping to find different housing. I did conduct interviews with both children after Mr. Farver was arrested and they both disclosed witnessing a lot of domestic violence between their father and Ms. Murray. Haylee disclosed that her father was very angry all the time and often scared her. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">I am requesting services be provided to Ms. Goodnow (who is aware this request is being made) as well as the children. They are both in need of mental health trauma counseling. Ms. Goodnow reported that David is diagnosed with ADHD and has not been on mediation since living with his father. Ms. Goodnow may also need assistance with finding housing to ensure the children can remain in her care. I am aware that she has income and is willing to move out of her current home. This is the address where she is currently residing. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Ms. Carol Goodnow</span></p><p>7466 East Furnace Branch Road</p><p>Glen Burnie, Maryland 21060</p><p>(410) 599-9105</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">I can be reached at 443-235-4942 or </span><a href=\"mailto:Katie.Beran@maryland.gov\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\">Katie.Beran@maryland.gov</a><span style=\"color: black;\"> with any questions or concerns. </span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">SN: Ms. Goodnow has No hx&nbsp;MJCS, NSOPW</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Hx under biofather:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">8008587&nbsp;22 CW&nbsp;INV&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 05 20</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Assign ROA to R. Young</p>",
